  "title": "Pruned combs and the associative spectrum of SC258",
  "batch_label": "新WIN-1批次",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "Let A={0,1,2} with binary operation whose rows, indexed by the left operand 0,1,2 and columns by the right operand 0,1,2, are (0,0,0), (1,1,0), (1,0,1). For every n>=1 let a_n count the distinct functions A^n -> A induced by all fully binary bracketings of x_1,...,x_n in that fixed order, using each variable exactly once and comparing on all inputs. Then a_1=a_2=1, a_3=2, and for every n>=4, a_n=3a_(n-1)-2a_(n-2)+a_(n-3). Equivalently, sum_(n>=1)a_n z^n=z(1-z)^2/(1-3z+2z^2-z^3). The proof also establishes that two such bracketings induce the same function exactly when their pruned labeled trees coincide, where pruning recursively deletes the right child of a node with two composite children and otherwise retains the node and prunes its children, without renumbering leaves.",
